From 2e54ae491a597ec17153479f07bf0cefbd074ed6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 22:30:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] first boot: let the password actually change, and finish
 removing QIS

FIELD REPORT (owner, RT-BE96U on v2.9.1, factory reset): admin/admin logged in,
the stock ASUS wizard appeared, the credentials entered there did not stick, and
the box returned to the login page. A second attempt reached the password page
and "would not take" a compliant password. No settings backup would restore.

ROOT CAUSE - a missing POST parameter, not a gate.
do_chpass_cgi (web.c) refuses with {"statusCode":"csrf"} unless http_id is
present WHILE THE PASSWORD IS STILL THE FACTORY DEFAULT. That gate arrived in
09b305504f, which in the same commit added http_id to the only caller that then
ran on a factory box - Reaper_FirstBoot.asp. ee76e21bcd deleted that page.
git log -S "http_id" -- Reaper_FirstBoot.asp returns exactly those two commits.
No surviving caller sent the token, so on a factory v2.9.1 box NEITHER
Main_Password.asp NOR the QIS wizard could change the admin password, and both
failed silently because the return value was discarded.

httpApi.chpass now supplies http_id itself, so no caller can omit it again
(**.js is do_ej processed - state.js already relies on that 170 times).
Main_Password.asp checks the result and reports 401/402/csrf instead of
navigating away as if it had worked.

THE SEVENTH GATE. v2.9.1 removed six first-boot redirects and left this one:
Main_Password.asp hopped to /QIS_wizard.htm?flag=wireless whenever w_Setting=="0"
- true on every factory box - and the new security banner linked straight at the
page that fires it. The wizard's own 3-second check_Auth.cgi poller then bounced
to /Main_Login.asp on any non-JSON reply. That is the whole reported loop. The
hop is gone; the page lands on "/". The same sweep removed the post-factory-reset
QIS landing in Restarting.asp, the network-map internet icon, the WAN-failure
page links and the disconnected-WAN hints in state.js. Repeater/AP/media-bridge/
WISP/MLO and op-mode paths still reference the wizard and are deliberately left
alone - none is on the router first-boot path, and a site-survey link is not a
WAN page.

WIRELESS BACK TO OPEN AT FACTORY (owner decision, made with the tradeoff stated).
v2.9.1 shipped wl_wpa_psk="admin" - five characters. hostapd's key handler
accepts 8..63 or a 64-hex key and otherwise leaves the value EMPTY, so wl0/wl1
got wpa_key_mgmt=WPA-PSK with no key line, hostapd refused the config
(ap_config.c "WPA-PSK enabled, but PSK or passphrase is not configured") and
exited - one instance serves every radio, so 6 GHz died with them despite its own
SAE config being valid. There is no hostapd watchdog on this model. That build had
no Wi-Fi on any band. Restored to the pre-2.9.1 values, which shipped and worked:
empty PSK, open, owe on 6 GHz. wl_crypto stays "aes" - unused while open, and
TKIP would cap an 11be radio to legacy rates.

Because factory is open again, ej_reaper_wifi_default had to change: it compared
only the PSK and deliberately skipped an empty one, so an open factory box read
as SECURED and cleared the banner's Wi-Fi row on exactly the boxes that needed
it. It now treats open/owe and an empty key as unsecured, and skips radios that
are switched off.

1ad324b104 IS REVERTED. All 18 of its defaults.c lines sit inside
"#if defined(EBG15) || defined(EBG19)" (defaults.c:5744..7030) and never compile
here; neither token appears in target.mak or .config. Proven by parsing
router_defaults[] out of the compiled defaults.o: no wl0/wl1/wl2_wpa_psk and no
wl3_* entry exists at all. The "per-unit block overrides the template" rule it
was written for does not hold on this fleet - wl_defaults() copies wl_* into each
wlN_* precisely because no per-unit entry is there.

ALSO:
- Main_Password.asp gains a current-password field, shown only when the password
  is already non-default. Without it the page was a dead end in that state: the
  blob demands cur_username/cur_passwd and 401s, and force_chgpass - its
  auth-bypass - is read in two places and written nowhere in the tree.
- Main_Password.asp moves from banner-only to css+banner injection. It rendered
  as raw stock ASUS, titled "ASUS Login"; that is what the field report called
  "the ASUS QIS". reaper_css_only[] is now tested before reaper_skip[] so the
  page stays un-bounced but is themed.
- do_reaper_restore_cgi gave ten distinct failures the same ek:"file", so a field
  report could not tell a truncated archive from a refused token from a full
  /jffs. ek keeps the coarse family; a new ec names the exact cause and the UI
  shows it in brackets.

No new dict tokens: the five reused ones are present in all 25 packs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
